From 91ea934f28a472d8d561796ee497c1ba0d8ac704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:11:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] feat(bin): standalone JSON-RPC-over-WebSocket client
 for the hermes /api/ws gateway

Per the captain's decision on state/hermes-vps-gateway.status: build the
standalone dispatch primitive now and defer fleet-dispatch wiring
(fm-spawn/fm-control/fm-crew-state/fm-busy-lib) to a follow-up task,
since those are entirely pane-shaped and a /api/ws session has no pane.

bin/fm-hermes-ws.py is a stdlib-only Python client (no third-party
dependency, matching fm-mail.py's existing stance) implementing the RFC
6455 handshake/framing from scratch, both loopback-token and gated
password-login -> cookie -> ws-ticket auth, and every session RPC named
in the brief (create/submit/status/history/steer/interrupt/close) plus a
dispatch convenience for smoke-testing. bin/fm-hermes-ws.sh resolves
FM_HERMES_WS_* config from the environment or $FM_HOME/.env, matching
fm-mail.sh's convention.

The wire protocol is grounded in the real v0.21.2 upstream source
(tui_gateway/ws.py, scripts/iso-certify.py's real first-party client),
not the earlier scout report's paraphrase. tests/fm-hermes-ws.test.sh
and its independently-written stub server (tests/fixtures/) prove the
client end to end over a real socket, offline. Not yet run against the
real VPS or any real Hermes install - still blocked on the captain's VPS
login credentials and an unconfirmed Origin-header requirement in gated
mode; see docs/verification/hermes.md.
